# Mikey & Don, Party Planners: "You may play lands and cast Mutant, Ninja, or Turtle spells from the top of your library. If you cast a creature spell this way, that creature
# enters with an additional +1/+1 counter on it." In turn 1 Bot1 casts Mikey & Don, plays the Island on top as its land play, then casts the Foot Elite (a Ninja, 2/4) now on
# top with Black Lotus: it enters a 3/5 with a counter. The Ornithopter under it is none of those types (it costs nothing, so only the permission could be missing): it may not be
# cast from the library. Memnite, cast from the hand, is the positive control for the counter: a 1/1 with none.

